    <!-- ===== Schedule-Approval Fields (environment-specific mapping + provisioning) ===== -->
    <section class="jim-admin-panel" data-panel="approvalfields">
        <h3>Schedule-Approval Fields / فیلدهای تایید تاریخ</h3>
        <p class="jim-admin-hint">
            The schedule-approval workflow (proposed completion date &rarr; approve/reject) needs five Jira
            custom fields. Historically their ids were hardcoded to the <strong>production</strong> instance, so
            the workflow could not work on this environment if the ids differ or the fields are missing.
        </p>
        <p class="jim-admin-hint">
            Each logical field resolves as: <strong>configured id</strong> (below) &rarr;
            <strong>production fallback id</strong> &rarr; <em>not configured</em>. So production keeps working with
            no configuration, while here you can either <strong>map</strong> an existing field or
            <strong>provision</strong> the missing ones. Provisioning is admin-only, cluster-safe, idempotent and
            audited &mdash; it never runs on startup.
        </p>
        <div id="jim-approval-status" class="jim-admin-hint"></div>

        <table class="aui" style="max-width:1080px;">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Field / فیلد</th>
                    <th>Logical key</th>
                    <th>Configured field id</th>
                    <th>Effective</th>
                    <th>Exists</th>
                    <th>Type</th>
                    <th>Options</th>
                    <th>Context</th>
                    <th>Screen</th>
                    <th>Fallback?</th>
                    <th></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="jim-approval-diag-rows">
                <tr><td colspan="11">Loading&hellip;</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Provision missing fields</h3>
        <p class="jim-admin-hint">
            Creates any field that neither the configured id nor the production fallback can resolve. Adopts an
            existing correctly-typed, same-named field instead of duplicating. Creates the
            <code>Pending / Approved / Rejected</code> options for the status field. Stores the resulting ids here.
            Running it again is safe (idempotent).
        </p>
        <div class="jim-admin-field">
            <label class="jim-admin-check">
                <input type="checkbox" id="jim-approval-add-screens"/>
                Also add created/adopted fields to Jira screens
            </label>
            <label class="jim-admin-label" for="jim-approval-screen-ids">Screen ids (comma separated; blank = Default Screen, id 1)</label>
            <input type="text" id="jim-approval-screen-ids" class="text" style="max-width:260px;" placeholder="1"/>
            <p class="jim-admin-hint" dir="rtl" lang="fa">
                فیلدهای گمشده به‌صورت ایمن و فقط با اقدام مدیر ساخته می‌شوند؛ اجرای دوباره باعث تکرار نمی‌شود.
                تغییری در پیکربندی تولید (production) بدون تایید صریح انجام نمی‌شود.
            </p>
            <div class="jim-admin-actions">
                <button id="jim-approval-refresh" type="button" class="aui-button">Refresh diagnostics</button>
                <button id="jim-approval-provision" type="button" class="aui-button aui-button-primary">Provision missing fields</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

